From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:43:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: mailbox: Enable the A7 ANS FIFOs on every start

The A7's ANS mailbox (AppleA7IOP V1) has its FIFOs enabled once, when
the mailbox probes. A client that restarts the coprocessor after system
sleep goes through apple_rtkit_reinit(), which stops and starts the
mailbox, and then needs the FIFOs on. On an iPad mini 2 (J85) the ANS
mailbox came back from s2idle with them off, although its power domain
read on.

Set needs_enable for the V1 variant as well, so apple_mbox_start()
enables them each time, as it does for the other A7 IOP mailboxes. At
the first start they are already on and the write changes nothing. The
A8 and A8X ANS mailboxes, on the generic match, are unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c b/drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c
index 16be0dbf5..390ecedf5 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/mailbox.c
@@ -536,6 +536,8 @@ static const struct apple_mbox_hw apple_mbox_a7iop_hw = {
  * its interrupt setup is a single enable write at +0x04. Its FIFOs
  * must be enabled at probe, before the client starts the IOP; the
  * V2 setup instead enables them when starting mailbox communication.
+ * They are enabled again on every start too: after system sleep the
+ * A7's ANS mailbox comes back with its FIFOs off.
  * The 64-bit endpoint/payload format and FIFO locations are shared.
  */
 static const struct apple_mbox_hw apple_mbox_a7iop_v1_hw = {
@@ -546,6 +548,7 @@ static const struct apple_mbox_hw apple_mbox_a7iop_v1_hw = {
 	.i2a_control = APPLE_A7IOP_MBOX_I2A_CONTROL,
 	.i2a_recv0 = APPLE_A7IOP_MBOX_I2A_RECV,
 	.packed_endpoint = true,
+	.needs_enable = true,
 	.needs_early_enable = true,
 	.has_irq_enable_only = true,
 	.irq_enable = 0x04,
